<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via three-day system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via three-day system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the banking system on Monday through three-day system repurchase agreements, a Fed spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>At 1130 EDT/1530 GMT, the normal time for Fed open market operations, the federal funds rate was trading at 5-3/8 percent, above the Fed's 5-1/4 percent target.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
